    <DataNode elementId="AT5G65720-MONOMER" textLabel="Cysteine desulfurase, mitochondrial" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT5G65720-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The presence of a mitochondrial form of cysteine desulfurase (AtNFS1) has been demonstrated in &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;. This result has been discussed as a proof for the existence of a conserved Fe/S-cluster biosynthesis in mitochondria which is probably linked to intracellular iron homeostasis |CITS:[11158531]|. Proteins involved in the sulfur (SUF) protein-mediated Fe-S cluster biogenesis such as AtSufE have been shown to induce both the mitochondrial (this gene) and the plastidic form of cysteine desulfursase |CITS:[16437155]|. Silencing of the plastidic cysteine desulfurase did not influence the mitochondrial form indicating that mitochondria and chloroplast have separate, crucial cysteine desulfurases and Fe-S cluster assembly mechanisms |CITS:[17372218]|.</Comment>
